    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "WHAT THIS DOES NOT SAY.\n\n1. It does not say the carrier is AXIOM-FREE. That is `Kernel::axiom_footprint`'s claim and is checked elsewhere; this fact is only that Lean's kernel accepts the declarations, whatever they rest on. A development full of axioms would replay just as happily.\n\n2. It does not say the `.lean` SOURCE artefact carries the whole carrier. It does not: Lean's elaborator refuses four declarations of it (two, plus two `unknown constant` cascades), because its reducer treats a `theorem` as opaque and `Nat.gcd`'s recursive step is justified by the theorem `Nat.mod_lt`. Re-spelling every `theorem` as `def` in the same file makes the elaborator accept the whole carrier in 27.9 s; that change is measured and deliberately not taken (ADR-0517).\n\n3. It does not say the 470 declarations are the RIGHT ones, only that Lean admits the ones there are. `creal_setoid_witness` is what stops the development being vacuous -- `Equiv.not_zero_one` and `not_le_one_zero` are exactly the declarations that make `CReal.Equiv` and `CReal.le` non-total, and they are two of the four the elaborator refuses.\n\n4. The number 470 is a snapshot of a carrier under active development; the fact's content is the EQUALITY of the two counts, and the checker compares them rather than either alone. It will need re-pinning when the carrier grows, which is the intended failure.",
